course: dictionary
lesson: 297
title: Ana: a name, an ending, a rare word
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Ana is most often a girl's name. It is a form of Anna and is common in Spanish and Portuguese. In a story or in your class, Ana is usually a person. «Ana was born in Colombia and looks different from her mum and dad.» Here Ana is a name, because it tells you about a person.
explain: The ending -ana can change the meaning of a word. «Victoriana» means things from Queen Victoria's time, and «Americana» means things typical of American culture. When you see -ana at the end of a word, ask: is this about a time, a place or a person?
explain: As a noun, ana is very rare. It means a collection of sayings or stories about someone. You will not meet it often, so use context: the words around it give the clues. Also remember that -ana can be just the end of a longer word, like banana or Montana. Do not split every word that ends that way.
fact: Ana is mostly a girl's name, a form of Anna.
fact: Ana is common in Spanish and Portuguese.
fact: The ending -ana means a collection of things about a person or place.
fact: «Victoriana» means things from Queen Victoria's time, and «Americana» means things typical of American culture.
fact: As a rare noun, «ana» means a collection of sayings or stories about someone.
exercise: In the sentence «Ana was born in Colombia», what kind of word is Ana? | *A name | A sweet | A type of bicycle | A town in Colombia
exercise: What does the ending -ana tell you about «Victoriana»? | *Things from Queen Victoria's time | Things from the sea | A girl's name | Sayings about a king
exercise: «It's wicked annoying,» Ana says («wicked» means very, in New England). What does wicked mean here? | Quiet and shy | Wet and cold | Evil and wicked | *Very
test: What does the ending -ana show in «Americana»? | A name for a girl | *Things typical of American culture | Things from the sea | A kind of bicycle
test: What should you do when -ana is only the end of a longer word, like «banana»? | Split it up and guess its meaning | Guess it is a name every time | *Read the whole word and use the context | Skip the sentence forever
exam: Which is the best check when you meet the rare noun «ana» in a sentence? | Guess it is a name every time | Ignore it because it is rare | *Read the words around it for clues and try your meaning in the sentence | Look only at the first letter
